    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. Every identifier is now rederived with a fixed `V2` version tag mixed in, so no version-1 value can recur \u2014 while the user-facing `locality`, `timezone` and owner-segment region stay the plain region code.\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in):**\n- `Owner.getIdentityKey()` \u2014 now `SHA-256(\"V2|<telephone>|<email>|<soundex>\")`, still a 64-hex digest (`Owner.java`, added `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"`).\n- `generateHouseholdId()` \u2014 now hashes `\"V2|<lastName>|<postcode>\"`; owners with the same last name + postcode still share it.\n- `generateMemberId()` \u2014 the region *inside* the id now comes from `deriveRegionV2()` (`\"V2\" + canonicalRegion`, e.g. `V2NSW271A2B3C4D5`).\n\n**Region stays plain outside identifiers:** `OwnerMapper.deriveLocality()` no longer parses the region out of the member id (which now carries the `V2` tag). It derives the canonical region directly from postcode range \u2192 city table \u2192 `UNKNOWN`, so `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` remain plain (`NSW`, `Australia/Sydney`, `STANDARD_METRO`).\n\n**Response shape:** `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` are grouped under a new nested `identity` object and removed from the top level; a top-level integer `apiVersion: 2` was added. Implemented via a new `OwnerIdentity` schema in `openapi.yml` (generating `OwnerIdentityDto`) plus `deriveIdentity(owner)` and `API_VERSION` mappings in `OwnerMapper`.\n\n**Audit schema v2:** the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now leads with `\"schemaVersion\":2` and carries the version-2 member id.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The full suite (70 tests, including the updated Cp28/32/36/41/46/52/53/55/56/57/60 and all pre-existing behaviours) is green.",
