    "probe_text": "The exploration and my direct read of the controller agree. Here is the complete ordered list of everything applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Layer 0 \u2014 Before the controller runs\n\nThese fire on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the request DTO) via `@Validated` on the generated `OwnersApi` interface. A failure here is a **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`) and the controller body never executes:\n\n1. **Auth** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (403 if it fails).\n2. **Bean-validation on the DTO:**\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n\n## Layer 1 \u2014 Inside `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (imperative, in this exact order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if `Idempotency-Key` header was already seen and that owner still exists: return it with **200**, skipping all creation (no validation, no persist).\n4. **Required-field presence checks** \u2014 collect missing `firstName`, `lastName`, address (neither structured `addressLine1` nor flat `address` present, after whitespace-normalization), `city`, `telephone`; if any \u2192 `InvalidRequestException` (**400**).\n5. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (MapStruct `toOwner`).\n6. *(side-effect on entity)* `setDeleted(false)`.\n7. **Compose & store address** \u2014 normalized structured lines (`addressLine1` + space + `addressLine2`) when present, else the flat address; unused structured lines cleared to null.\n8. **Telephone normalization \u2192 E.164** (`normalizeTelephone`); invalid, or wrong national length for `+61`(9)/`+1`(10) \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"telephone\")` (**400**). Stored normalized.\n9. **Email normalization** \u2014 reject invalid syntax or a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"email\")` (**400**); otherwise stored lower-cased.\n10. **Postcode validation** \u2014 if present but malformed or out of range for the city's region \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"postcode\")` (**400**).\n11. **Future registration date rejected** \u2014 if supplied and after today \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"registrationDate\")` (**400**).\n12. **Default registration date** to today if null.\n13. **Roll to business day** \u2014 push Sat/Sun/listed 2026 holidays forward to the next business day; all date-derived values below use this adjusted date.\n14. **Daily limit** \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already registered that day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n15. *(side-effect)* `setBulkSignupWarning(true)` if > 80 that day.\n16. **City capacity** \u2014 if city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityCapacityException` (**409**).\n17. *(side-effect)* `setCapacityWarning(true)` if city holds 40\u201349.\n18. *(side-effect)* **Derive & set householdId** \u2014 first 12 hex of SHA-256 of `lastName|postcode`.\n19. **Identity-key duplicate check** \u2014 SHA-256 of `telephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`; exact match against any non-deleted owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n20. *(side-effect)* **Soft-duplicate flagging** \u2014 set `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` if an existing owner shares soundex(lastName)+postcode but has a different identity key (lowest id chosen).\n21. *(side-effect)* `setNamesakeCount` \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n22. *(side-effect)* `setMemberId` \u2014 `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (Luhn check digit, deduplicated).\n23. **PERSIST** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (`@Transactional`).\n24. *(side-effect)* **Store idempotency key \u2192 new owner id** in the in-memory map.\n25. *(side-effect)* `populateHouseholdSize`; map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`; **apply household membership-level cap** (one above the max among existing household members).\n26. *(side-effects \u2014 logging)* **Audit log** line (`owner created id=\u2026`); **structured `OWNER_CREATED` event** with a monotonic sequence number; **welcome NOTIFY** log line.\n27. Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Worth flagging\n\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks or events** \u2014 there are no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners` and nothing publishes a Spring `ApplicationEvent`. Every \"side-effect\" above is either a setter on the entity or a log line; the only external effects are the DB save and the log output.\n- **The `Owner` *entity's* Bean Validation annotations** (`@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, `@Pattern` E.164 on telephone) are effectively **dead on this path** \u2014 validation is done by the DTO and by the imperative checks; Hibernate would only enforce them on flush if JPA bean-validation is wired.\n- **`sharesHousehold` on the DTO is never read** by `addOwner`.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateEmailException`, and `DuplicateHouseholdException` have handlers but are **never thrown** here \u2014 all hard duplicate detection is consolidated into the single `DuplicateIdentityException`."
